    "Main woman (navy buttoned top, gray shorts, ponytail) | walking toward camera, left hand gripping blue umbrella shaft, right hand holding red fruit at chest level | near camera in left profile, still holding umbrella and fruit | continuous walk with natural gait; around 00:04 the fruit moves from chest grip to resting against her right hand and the umbrella shaft; left-hand grip on shaft never released",
    "Blue umbrella | open canopy, shaft held in woman's left hand with visible wrapped grip (ring on ring finger) | still gripped at end, canopy exits top of frame as camera zooms | no release, no shaft clipping through hand or body; shaft passes in front of her chest/neck area consistently with a forward-held umbrella",
    "Red round fruit | gripped in woman's right hand at chest | resting at base of her spread right-hand fingers with umbrella shaft directly behind it | contact with right hand visible in every frame (00:00, 00:02, 00:04, 00:06, 00:08); supported by hand and/or shaft throughout, no floating or unsupported interval",
    "Foreground pedestrians (teal-shirt woman, man with shoulder bag, bald man in dark shirt) | crossing between camera and main subject | exit frame edges | normal occlusion passes; no visible interpenetration with the main woman or stalls"
